# stub-claude-fixtures.manifest — the reviewed disposition of every test file
# that builds its own `claude` stub. your-org/nexus-code#764.
#
# Columns (TAB-separated):
#   1 path          repo-relative
#   2 step          which resolver step the CONSTRUCTION lands on: local|path
#   3 claude-bin    does the file assign CLAUDE_BIN?
#   4 guard         does it call th_require_stub_claude?
#   5 disposition   pinned | no-resolver | exposed | selftest
#   6 reason        why that disposition — required, and reviewed
#
# Columns 1-4 are FACTS, regenerated by `stub-claude-fixtures.sh`; column 5-6 are
# the human verdict. `test-stub-claude-manifest.sh` fails when 1-4 drift from the
# classifier, so a NEW fixture that stubs `claude` lands here unclassified and red.
#
# COLUMN 5 IS NOT FREE-FORM — IT IS ENTAILED BY COLUMNS 2-3 (your-org/nexus-code#1076).
# The verdict used to be checked for MEMBERSHIP in the set above and nothing more,
# so a recognised-but-WRONG verdict passed — and the blind direction was the
# permissive one: relabelling `test-integration/_harness.sh` from `exposed` to
# `pinned` deleted the only rule enforced about the repo's single genuinely
# exposed site while every assertion still passed. The closure now asserted:
#
#   exposed      => path + no-claude-bin + guarded
#   no-resolver  => path + no-claude-bin, AND a dated `reach=0` (its whole evidence)
#   pinned       => local OR claude-bin  — `pinned` is structurally impossible
#                   for a path+no-claude-bin fixture
#   selftest     => this suite's own row, and no other. The exemption is pinned to
#                   one path so it cannot become an escape hatch that re-opens
#                   `#1076` by another spelling.
#   anything else => REFUSED (default-deny, not a permissive fall-through)
#
# COLUMN 6: A STATED MEASUREMENT MUST NAME THE BLOB IT WAS TAKEN ON
# (your-org/nexus-code#1241). `reach` is a property of a BLOB, so a bare
# `reach=N` asserts something about a tree nobody named and rots silently — a
# stated `reach=25` measured 29 ten commits later, and nothing noticed. Required
# form, enforced:
#
#   reach=<N> @blob <sha>          as in the test-spawn-worker.sh row below.
#
# The shas below were DERIVED FROM THIS FILE'S OWN HISTORY — for each row, the
# blob its path had at the commit that first stated that row's current `reach`
# value — not invented and not back-filled with today's blob, which would have
# asserted measurements nobody took. Consequently many rows are HONESTLY STALE
# today; the suite names them on every run rather than failing, because this repo
# ships no instrument that re-derives `reach`, all 36 listed files were touched in
# the last 90 days (293 commits), and a red whose cheapest resolution is to bump a
# sha without re-measuring manufactures false provenance. Re-measure, then re-date.
#
# THE AXIS. `monitor/_claude-bin.sh` resolves `$CLAUDE_BIN` -> then
# `$NEXUS_ROOT/node_modules/.bin/claude` -> then PATH. The `#746` hazard
# (`locals-env.sh` re-fronting `$NEXUS_LOCALS/bin` via BASH_ENV) can only bite at
# the PATH step. So:
#
#   pinned       construction decides the resolution before PATH is consulted —
#                either CLAUDE_BIN (step 1) or the fixture's own
#                node_modules/.bin/claude under its own NEXUS_ROOT (step 2).
#                Immune by construction, whether or not it reaches the resolver.
#   no-resolver  step 3, but MEASURED never to reach `_claude-bin.sh` at all.
#   exposed      step 3 AND reaches the resolver. MUST call th_require_stub_claude.
#   selftest     drives the guard's own pass and refuse arms on purpose.
#
# HOW REACHABILITY WAS ESTABLISHED. Not by reading. `_claude-bin.sh` was
# instrumented with an entry trace and a fail-closed interlock, and every member
# was executed under a decoy nexus whose `claude` is a stub (so the hazardous
# re-fronting stayed active but no billed binary was reachable). The REACH counts
# below are measured; `reach=0` means the resolver was never sourced. Two arms
# proved the instrument fires: `test-spawn-worker-resume.sh` traced 34 reaches,
# and `test-respawn-loop-integration.sh` resolved to the DECOY locals copy rather
# than its own stub — the hazard reproducing, and its guard refusing.
#
# VERDICT ON THE ISSUE'S CANDIDATE LIST OF 22: none of the 22 is `exposed`.
# 16 are `pinned`, 5 are `no-resolver`, and one — `test-version-restart-self.sh` —
# creates no `claude` stub at all (the grep matched `install-claude-local.sh`), so
# it is absent below. The two genuinely exposed sites are the one `#759` already
# fixed and `test-integration/_harness.sh`, which the list does not contain.
#
monitor/watcher/test-agent-delivery-address-space.sh	path	claude-bin	unguarded	pinned	Passes CLAUDE_BIN=$WORK/bin/claude on every spawn (the single spawn() helper is the only invocation path), so step 1 decides before PATH is consulted and the #746 re-fronting cannot bite; the stub exists only because CI has no claude and spawn-worker.sh refuses without one.
monitor/watcher/test-bootstrap-claude-install.sh	local	claude-bin	unguarded	pinned	Passes CLAUDE_BIN explicitly per run and drives the resolver's fail-loud arm; reach=0 @blob f47ba02 @127ff1f (bootstrap stubbed).
monitor/watcher/test-cc-auto-update.sh	local	no-claude-bin	unguarded	pinned	Since #1002 (w239 bundle) make_root plants a pin-following stub at $root/node_modules/.bin/claude under its own fixture root (the drift assertion needs the resolver's own answer), so step 2 beats PATH; the older $root/claude via CC_AUTO_CLAUDE_BIN remains for the verbs that pass it. Was path/no-resolver before #1002; re-classified local/pinned at the bundle head.
monitor/watcher/test-cc-gate.sh	local	no-claude-bin	unguarded	pinned	Since #1002 (w239 bundle) the --keep-prefix and cch_stage_candidate cases plant a stub claude under the fixture's own prefix/node_modules/.bin (the helper verifies the staged binary IS the candidate), so step 2 beats PATH; a stub npm on a private PATH does the install. Enrolled at the bundle head.
monitor/watcher/test-cc-restart-watchdog-loop.sh	local	no-claude-bin	unguarded	pinned	Stub at $root/node_modules/.bin/claude under its own root; step 2 beats PATH; reach=0 @blob c8528f7 @127ff1f.
monitor/watcher/test-cc-restart-watchdog-verify.sh	local	no-claude-bin	unguarded	pinned	Stub at $root/node_modules/.bin/claude under its own root; step 2 beats PATH; reach=0 @blob fe4f074 @127ff1f.
monitor/watcher/test-claude-loop.sh	path	claude-bin	unguarded	pinned	Passes CLAUDE_BIN=$STUB_BIN/claude on every invocation; measured reach=10 @blob 3d47231 @127ff1f, all resolving to that stub via step 1.
monitor/watcher/test-entry.sh	path	no-claude-bin	unguarded	no-resolver	Stub exists so a pane process is NAMED claude for entry.sh's liveness walk; nothing spawns it through the resolver; reach=0 @blob 6a55170 @127ff1f.
monitor/watcher/test-gh-identity.sh	local	no-claude-bin	unguarded	pinned	Empty node_modules/.bin/claude only so a link-nexus-tools precondition holds; step 2; reach=0 @blob 81516e9 @127ff1f.
monitor/watcher/test-install-claude-local.sh	local	no-claude-bin	unguarded	pinned	The npm symlink IS the artifact under test; step 2 path by definition; reach=0 @blob 903c537 @127ff1f.
monitor/watcher/test-install-shell-hook.sh	path	no-claude-bin	unguarded	no-resolver	Fake locals/bin/claude proves the rc hook puts `claude` on PATH by name; asserts PATH resolution directly, never _claude-bin.sh; reach=0 @blob a9b799b @127ff1f.
monitor/watcher/test-instance-heartbeat.sh	local	no-claude-bin	unguarded	pinned	Stub at node_modules/.bin/claude as a spawn precondition; step 2; reach=0 @blob 132b505 @127ff1f.
