monitor/watcher/test-skeptic-arm-recording.sh	local	claude-bin	unguarded	pinned	Two stub sources, and column 3 is claude-bin because of the SECOND. (a) $fn/node_modules/.bin/claude built by _mk_nexus per fake nexus, under the fixture's OWN NEXUS_ROOT -- step 2, three _run_spawn invocations (5a default, 5b recursive, 5c no-r) at :432/:450/:461. (b) NEW (your-org/nexus-code#1356): the #1251 BEHAVIOURAL block at :764 runs the real spawn-worker.sh with CLAUDE_BIN pinned to $_sb1251/claude -- step 1, decided before node_modules or PATH. measured reach=4 @blob 709d1c4d @42e3dba9, and `pinned` stays entailed twice over (vstep==local AND vpin==claude-bin). NOTE this row was ALREADY STALE before #1356: commit 82c66dbe added the :753 invocation on 2026-09-01 and did not teach this manifest, so the previously-stated count of three described a tree that no longer existed. Why the pin exists: spawn-worker.sh:773 sources _claude-bin.sh unconditionally, far above the -r check at :2020, so on a runner with no node_modules and no claude on PATH the assertion measured CLAUDE RESOLUTION (rc 1) instead of the -r gate (rc 9) -- red in every CI band since 82c66dbe.
